

Usage:	ASMCOP	asmfile [,asmfile ...] [@cmdfile]  [options]

/Aserrorfile[=file]	- enable source error file [default extension = .ase]
/NOAserrorfile		- disable source error file
/CHip=chip              - specify chip= COPxxx | xxx | ANYCOP  
/[NO]CNDDirectives	- enable/disable listing of conditional directives
/[NO]CNDLines		- enable/disable listing of conditional lines
/[NO]COMMentlines	- enable/disable listing of comment lines
/[NO]COMPlexrel 	- enable/disable complex relocation
/[NO]CONstants		- enable/disable constants appearing in symbol table
/[NO]Crossref		- enable/disable cross reference table listing
/[NO]DAtadirectives	- enable/disable listing of more than the first line
			  of data generating directives, e.g. .db
/Define symbol[=value]	- set symbol to a value.  If no value, set to 1
/[NO]ECho		- enable/disable echoing of command files
/Errorfile[=file]	- enable error file [default extension = .err].
/NOErrorfile		- disable error file
/[NO]Formfeed		- enable/disable formfeeds between listing pages
/[NO]Headings		- enable/disable headings on each page
/[NO]ILines		- enable/disable line numbers on include files
/Include=directory	- specify directory for include file search


?+


/Listfile[=file]	- specify listing file [default extension = .lis]
/NOListfile		- disable listing file
/[NO]LOcalsymbols	- enable/disable local symbols in symbol table and
			  object module
/[NO]Masterlist 	- enable/disable master listing flag
/[NO]MCAlls		- enable/disable listing of macro calls
/[NO]MCOmments		- enable/disable listing of macro comment lines
/[NO]MDefinitions	- enable/disable listing of macro definitions
/[NO]MEMory		- enable/disable using memory for optimization
/[NO]MExpansions	- enable/disable listing of macro expansions
/[NO]MLocals		- enable/disable  macro local symbols in symbol table
/[NO]MObject		- enable/disable listing of lines in macros which
			  generate code
/MODel=S | M | L	- override default memory model; Small, Medium, Large
/Numberlines		- lines have same line number as position in file
/NONumberlines		- all lines have sequential line numbers
/Objectfile[=file]	- specify object file [default extension = .obj]
/NOObjectfile		- inhibit object file
/PAss=count | ALL	- set number of passes. PASS=ALL means assembler will
			  take as many passes as necessary to optimize code.
			  PASS=2 is assembly without optimization.


?+



/PLength=length 	- set page length
/PWidth=width		- set page width
/Quick			- perform errors only assembly. No object file, list
			  file or symbol table is produced.  Only errors are
			  listed.
/[NO]Remove		- enable/disable removal of error lines produced by
			  the /Aserrorfile option.
/REStore		- restore flags saved by /SAve control
/SAve			- save all control flags
/SIGnedcompare		- >, >=, < , <= operators use signed compare
/NOSIGnedcompare	- >, >=, < , <= operators use unsigned compare
/SIZesymbol=size	- set maximum symbol size
/SYm_debug		- generate symbolic debug information
/[NO]Tablesymbols	- enable/disable symbol table listing
/[NO]TABS		- enable/disable tabs in output listing. /NOTABS
			  implies all tabs will be converted to appropriate
			  numbers of blanks.
/Undefine symbol	- undefine symbol defined with /Define control
/[NO]UPpercase		- enable/disable uppercase conversion for symbols
/[NO]Verify		- enable/disable output listing on all passes
/[NO]Warnings		- enable/disable warning messages
/[NO]Xdirectory 	- enable/disable searching standard directories for
			  include files

?-
